llvm-3.7.1 forward port: a field of a struct declared with an alignment is aligned as the struct is

This patch CHANGES THE ALIGNMENT clang gives a member access when the
member's struct or class carries an alignment attribute (alignas,
__attribute__((aligned))): the alignment of the load or store is the base
object's alignment at the field's offset, where 3.7.1 takes the field
type's own alignment. It is one number of upstream r246985 (7f416cc42638,
2015-09-08, "Compute and preserve alignment more faithfully in
IR-generation", first released in 3.8.0), which computes a field's address
as the base Address's alignment at the field's offset for every struct
(CodeGenFunction::EmitLValueForField through emitAddrOfFieldStorage and
CGBuilder's CreateStructGEP). The commit itself is the Address type through
all of clang's IR generation (110 files) and is NOT ported; this is its
number for one case, written into 3.7.1's EmitLValueForField, and exists in
no upstream state: a narrowing of this project.

What the base shows. A 16-aligned vector of four floats copied or set
field by field (0x13d01e0 and its three siblings, 0x13d90d0, 0x13544e0):
the merged 16-byte move is `vmovaps`, which needs the first field's access
to say align 16; 3.7.1 says align 4 and the move is `vmovups`. The
prebuilt 3.8.1 and 3.9.1 give `vmovaps` (round 273B, b273/f3/).

Why not upstream's rule for every struct. Built alone and swept (round
276B, variant fieldalign_all: the same statement without the attribute
test): the six rows become equal and 132 rows are lost, 148 functions
change: an int member at an 8-aligned offset is loaded `align 8`, and
3.7.1's GVN then widens that load to cover its neighbour (the load
widening upstream removed in 4.0.0), which the base does not do. Round
274D counted the same class under the prebuilt 3.8.1 (130 rows). So the
base's compiler has neither 3.8's rule with 3.8's GVN nor 3.7.1's number
for the aligned vector. Not measured: upstream's rule for every struct
together with 4.0.0's removal of the load widening.

Swept alone over the game module built by the installed 3.7.1 with its
eight patches (round 276B, 5,497 rows, 6,659 functions): 7 functions
change; 6 rows become equal (5,476 to 5,482: 0x13d01e0, 0x13d0210,
0x13d0240, 0x13d0270, 0x13d90d0, 0x13544e0) and none is lost; the seventh
function is the draft 0x4b32c0 (0 of 19 before and after).

--- a/tools/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGExpr.cpp
+++ b/tools/clang/lib/CodeGen/CGExpr.cpp
@@ -2709,6 +2709,16 @@
   if (!base.getAlignment().isZero())
     alignment = std::min(alignment, base.getAlignment());
 
+  // A field of a struct declared with an alignment is aligned as the struct
+  // is at the field's offset.
+  if (!rec->isUnion() && rec->hasAttr<AlignedAttr>() &&
+      !base.getAlignment().isZero()) {
+    CharUnits offset = getContext().toCharUnitsFromBits(
+        getContext().getASTRecordLayout(rec).getFieldOffset(
+            field->getFieldIndex()));
+    alignment = base.getAlignment().alignmentAtOffset(offset);
+  }
+
   bool mayAlias = rec->hasAttr<MayAliasAttr>();
 
   llvm::Value *addr = base.getAddress();
